title The fall is a product, and the narrowest head returned the most
prompt Take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, Standfast on reds first, read one council-rota row, send the increment
think Standfast first. Read crux/REDS.md end to end -- rows %142, %143, and %144 each carry a CLOSED line, and no row in the ledger stands open. The line is clear, so constructive work may begin.
think Running thread from session-logs/README.md and the newest three recommend lines -- the Caravan ladder lift arc, with found_path named as the fall head at 375 and mend_the_plan still leading by carry at 684 for a return of only 72. The fall queue stays the one to read.
think Read the family by hand before lifting, which is what REDS %140 and %144 both cost the arc when it was skipped. Sixteen rungs hold fn found_path byte for byte at twenty-eight lines, confirmed by md5 across all sixteen. Three callers per rung, all staying in the rung. Every rung already imports ladder_checks.
think The body reaches addressable, reader_dir, max_note_path_len, and NoteError, and the reach meter prices all four at zero -- every one already public in all sixteen rungs. So the lift widens nothing of any kind, and the hand-read agrees with the meter rather than correcting it.
think Lifted the body into caravan/ladder_checks.rye beside ask_path as pub fn found_path(comptime rung: type, buf, address), the fifth member of the reader-box path family after hand_path, tell_path, renew_path, and ask_path. Each of the sixteen rungs now calls it through a three-line stub.
think The comptime assert holding suffix.len == ".outof".len travelled with the body. That is the clearest case this arc has met of a rule sixteen files could quietly come to disagree about: two suffixes that must stay one width so a finding lands in the same box, at the same width, as the word about how that reader's quarrel came out.
obs Carry measured 61,560 -> 61,185 after the lift -- exactly 375, the number the scan formula returned before the lap began. Five laps running the arithmetic has named the fall before the meter read it.
obs The finding worth carrying is the arithmetic itself, which this row settled rather than merely illustrated. A fall is the count of rungs past the first multiplied by the lines a stub returns. Both factors trade freely and neither is privileged, so a family too narrow to look important returns as much as a wide one whose body runs short. This row asked exactly that question and answered it by returning more than the wider row folded before it.
obs The carry queue and the fall queue disagree because carry counts every copy of a body while a fall counts only the copies past the first, less the stub each leaves behind. That is why the fall queue has found the next row before the carry queue for five laps: carry measures what a family holds, and a fall measures what a lift returns.
obs The copy witness caught two unheld numbers this lap and both left the prose. A sentence naming twenty-five lines and thirty-one rungs recited two counts no assert in either file holds, which is REDS %110 exactly, and the spelled-number reader built to close REDS %143 is what saw them. Both witnesses now state the rule and let the asserted numbers carry it.
obs The fall queue has reached a plateau rather than a standout. bearing_note leads at 342, appraisal_note stands at 333, answered_by at 330, and recant_note at 324 -- three of the four are a twelve-line note over thirty-seven to thirty-nine rungs, each widening nothing. All four now stand asserted in the reach witness, so the plateau is a measurement rather than an impression.
obs The council rota row read this lap was Water and Venus -- care and flow. Gall's Law landed on the work directly: this arc grows one lifted body at a time out of a ladder that was already green, rather than designing the whole harness first. The happy zone and the thin edge read on it too -- a lifted body is one place a contract lives instead of sixteen, which is the seam discipline arriving as a refactoring rather than as a test.
